// The HPA of every application container and of the gateway (DESIGN.md AB2, AB10): SimOxide's
// HorizontalPodAutoscaler with Kubernetes' defaults, CPU target 0.7, 2 to 50 pods, 2 at the start,
// a new pod ready after 30 s; cost counts the pods the simulation measured.
autoscaler : Autoscaling {
    targetUtilisation = 0.7
    maxReplicas       = 50
    minReplicas       = 2
    startupSeconds    = 30.0
    initialReplicas   = 2
}

// C's `day` profile (DESIGN.md C4, AB3): A compressed day (DLIM: seasonal part + bursts): a low
// browsing night, a morning ramp, midday shopping with a short burst (C: 60-s peaks of 1.9 x), a
// sale spike with the ordering mix (SPIKE: volume and mix change together; BURST), an evening
// peak, a browsing decline. volume = sessions relative to the realistic workload's design
// sessions; admin stays constant. The first 120 s warm up and are not measured. Per session class
// a step per phase (factor = volume x the class's share in the phase's mix / its share in the base
// mix; admin keeps the model's rate). Measured from 120 s to 1320 s; seeds 1..5 (5 simulations per
// evaluation, AB26), usage streams, at most 400 pods created (else infeasible).
profile : LoadProfile {
    warmUpSeconds = 120.0
    endSeconds    = 1320.0
    name          = "day"
    seed          = 1
    usageStreams  = true
    maxPods       = 400
    replications  = 5
}
